 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Bosch HBS534BS0B oven displaying E011 and won't let me do anything. Beeping. Help!"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "While I cannot find an exact public mapping for 'E011' on this specific model, in many Bosch ovens this code typically indicates a fault with the internal temperature sensor (thermistor) or its connection to the main control board. To help narrow this down, please try resetting the oven by switching it off at the wall and leaving it for about 5 minutes before turning it back on. If the error persists immediately, it is likely a hardware fault (sensor or PCB). Does the error appear as soon as you turn it on, or only when you try to set a cooking temperature? Also, does the oven heat up at all if you ignore the code and select a function?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Switched it off at the cooker switch for 5 mins and it came back up normally with no code. I tried it afterwards and it heated to 180C fine. Was the error likely just a glitch?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Yes, it was almost certainly a transient glitch. These codes can sometimes appear due to minor voltage fluctuations or momentary sensor communication hiccups that clear themselves on a power cycle. You should be fine to use it as normal; just keep an eye on whether the code returns frequently."
  }
 ],
